<title>JAPAN: Japan drug firms up as investors seek forex haven.</title>
<headline>Japan drug firms up as investors seek forex haven.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Japanese pharmaceutical firms rose in Wednesday morning trade, as investors bought shares in defensive sectors which are relatively unaffected by currency fluctuations.</p>
<p>As of 0120 GMT, Yamanouchi Pharmaceutical Co Ltd was up 30 yen at 3,030 after hitting a new high for calendar 1997 of 3,040.</p>
<p>Takeda Chemical Industries Ltd was up 20 yen at 3,100 after hitting a new calendar year high of 3,110 yen.</p>
</text>
